The code statements that lead to the bug are:
cancel_work_sync(&client_data->work_ishtp_reset);
cancel_work_sync(&client_data->work_ec_evt);
cros_ish_deinit(cros_ish_cl);
Reason: These lines in the remove function deinitialize the ISHTP client without first unregistering the EC device. The missing call to cros_ec_unregister() means sub-devices (such as the cros_ec_console_log_work kthread) are not synchronously shut down, so after unbinding the driver the kthread continues to access freed device memory, causing a use-after-free crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
+	cros_ec_unregister(client_data->ec_dev);
Reason: This line is added before cros_ish_deinit() to properly unregister the EC device. Calling cros_ec_unregister() synchronously shuts down all sub-devices, including the console log work kthread, ensuring no background threads access freed memory after the driver is removed, thus preventing the use-after-free.

